<!-- WHY VNG -->
<section class="why-section" id="why-vng">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="why-header r-left">
      <div class="tag">Why VNG</div>
      <h2>Built different.<br>On purpose.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="why-grid stagger">
      <div class="why-card r">
        <div class="why-icon">01</div>
        <h3>The Mid-Market Sweet Spot</h3>
        <p>Most contractors are either too small to be reliable or too big to actually care about your project. VNG sits in the middle on purpose — the systems and bench depth of a large firm with the speed and flexibility of a specialist crew. Your project gets real attention from people who treat your deadline like their own.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why-card r">
        <div class="why-icon">02</div>
        <h3>One Throat to Choke</h3>
        <p>All trades under one contract. When something goes sideways — and on any project, something will — you call one number. We don't point fingers at subs or blame the schedule. We own the outcome, period. That's not a sales line. It's how we've built a reputation over a thousand projects.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="why-card r">
        <div class="why-icon">03</div>
        <h3>Deadline Is Non-Negotiable</h3>
        <p>We treat your handover date as a hard constraint, not a target. When a project falls behind, we don't send an update and hope — we scale crew, extend hours, and resequence trades before we ask for more time. Your opening date, your tenant's move-in, your client's expectations — they don't move.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

